{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please","id":906,"title":"Less Plot, More Choices, Please?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T22:03:26-07:00","id":906,"title":"Less Plot, More Choices, Please?","content":"I really hope that Trinity.2 is going to be less plot-based than Trinity itself was. Part of that means it'd be really awesome to have all nine Psi Orders in the corebook, fully playable. Then if you want to have <i>optional</i> metaplot stuff like the loss of contact with the Extrasolar Colonies, the destruction of the Chibs and the disappearance of the Upeo, that's awesome! But please, let the Storytellers decide what material they do and don't want in their games instead of writing everything into the books.<br /> <br /> With each setting being distinct in time, a leap of almost 100 years between Adventure!, Aberrant and Aeon, obviously there are going to be some setting assumptions. The Age of Adventure! evolved into the Nova Age and the Novas went insane and ushered in the post-apocalyptic-new-world of the Psions. That's cool. It'd just be nice for the settings to stay pretty static instead of having things like the Upeo returning in the &quot;middle&quot; of the gameline. It's even weird that there <i>is</i> a &quot;middle&quot; of the game line. Like it's a novel and you have to buy all the &quot;ploty&quot; books to understand the &quot;real&quot; setting. Can we just cram all the default assumptions into the cores, have as many playable options as possible then release some of those awesome and badass tiny-tiny books like the Field Reports that have &quot;metaplot&quot; updates? I'd be all for a book about how to run the Chitra Bhanu Purge, or the Disappearance of the Teleporters. I just would prefer that to be optional stuff. I get that it adds tension to the plot.. but I'd rather be the one adding tension to the plot that I made for my players instead of following the plot the writers are creating for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T23:59:07-07:00","id":960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please#post906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then if you want to have <i>optional</i> metaplot stuff like the loss of contact with the Extrasolar Colonies, the destruction of the Chibs and the disappearance of the Upeo, that's awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not metaplot, that's backstory.<br /> <br /> Since this isn't a generic sci-fi game, we're still going to include backstory. It's an intrinsic part of what makes this a distinctive setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T00:32:21-07:00","id":977,"title":"","content":"It feels a lot like Metaplot when two of those three get reversed in later books. The Extra-Solar colonies are re-contacted and the Upeo return. It'd be nice to have the <i>removal</i> of playable groups take place in optional books, instead of that limitation being the default assumption of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T01:13:54-07:00","id":985,"title":"","content":"Groups that aren't playable at first and become playable later exist for 2 reasons within an RPG.<br /> 1. To sell their inevitable splat book that details them and their powers.<br /> 2. because the writers haven't found a worth while way to use said groups correctly within the established setting books.<br /> <br /> I'd like to believe that Ian is going to run this ship correctly. part of running it correctly is making it have some ability to make profit. that means, on some level, selling splat books. I dunno what the Roi for splats with just adventure material in them..but I'm sure it's low enough that most of those books sell on drive thru for less than 10 bucks each. If they hold back a group that might be playable at some point, then people who want to play that group will purchase the books, and thus more money for both the game line, and the company, more perceived interest, and more books get written. <br /> <br /> It seems unfair maybe, to not have every group in the entire game available from the start, but it's been that way for years within the RPG industry, and I'm not sure why we're holding OP/WW to any sort of different standard. <br /> <br /> Hey man, be thankful he's not making the Aeonverse D20..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T01:17:13-07:00","id":988,"title":"","content":"That's true, I know he has to be able to sell Psi Order books. But seriously, <b>teleporters</b> not being playable by default? That's one of the big three psychic powers anyone ever wants. Telepathy, Telekinesis and Teleportation. The other, weird stuff like Biokinesis or, <i>sigh</i> even Quantakinesis (which isn't even a thing) is understandable to leave for later books. But... dude. <i><b>Teleporting!</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T01:30:52-07:00","id":995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=977#post977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels a lot like Metaplot when two of those three get reversed in later books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That those events are reversed is metaplot. That those events exist in the first place is not.<br /> <br /> Gangrel being part of the Camarilla is backstory. Gangrel leaving the Camarilla is metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T01:33:59-07:00","id":996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=988#post988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even Quantakinesis (which isn't even a thing)</div> </div> </div> </div>Google &quot;micro-PK&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T02:06:50-07:00","id":999,"title":"","content":"I love the Chibs <i>so much, </i>but I can really understand them being gone by the time the setting starts, and Quantakinesis has way less audience attraction even if there is the general <i>idea</i> of manipulating sub-atomic particles and forces via psionics. Teleporation, however, is a huge pop culture and scifi fixture. I really feel like the Upeo at least should be included in the corebook as a playable group, even if it's mentioned in the setting part that they're not present on Earth at the moment.<br /> <br /> It's always such a bummer to get a new RPG and flip through, see this awesome group and then read the depressing part: NOT PLAYABLE. And worse to later have them become playable, so it feels like the only reason they weren't playable in the first place was so they could be introduced later as part of a metaplot story arc. Even if that wasn't why, that's how it felt to me. I really don't like having the metaplot of a game determine what I can and can't play or use in my games. I wanna do that. Trinity, all three games, had awesome background and setting...but sometimes I felt like it came at the cost of letting the Storytellers make their own choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T02:30:03-07:00","id":1003,"title":"","content":"I don't mind an Order being purged but would prefer that such a purge be left up to the individual storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:07:55-07:00","id":1247,"title":"","content":"The trouble with backstory in a game set in multiple time periods with each one being playable and each one being tied to the others and, moreover, the middle one being essentially all about having the power to change the world and alter the court of history is that it becomes really hard to do and stick with the canon.<br /> <br /> Which is why, in my opinion, the books should encourage us to not even try. Play Aberrant and go nuts, everything that is purported to happen in this timeline can and will change, but are good sources of ideas. Metaplot is a plot which is advancing through the line, which Trinity won't be (I imagine), but a set timeline does make it tricky for GMs, especially if your characters in Aberrant become really powerful. Which they will, and then start changing everything, which they arguably actually should be doing since that's kind of the whole point of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T16:36:08-07:00","id":1374,"title":"","content":"That's something I was hoping someone would bring up. Is it at all possible to just have Aberrant's official policy be...I don't know if this makes sense, but the story going forwards rather than backwards? So in Aeon, the Aberrant War happened, but if you're playing Aberrant you don't have to work that in if you don't want to. Likewise maybe Adventure can thwart Aberrant's beginnings right from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T19:52:55-07:00","id":1456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=988#post988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, I know he has to be able to sell Psi Order books. But seriously, <b>teleporters</b> not being playable by default? That's one of the big three psychic powers anyone ever wants. Telepathy, Telekinesis and Teleportation. The other, weird stuff like Biokinesis or, <i>sigh</i> even Quantakinesis (which isn't even a thing) is understandable to leave for later books. But... dude. <i><b>Teleporting!</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I've read comics and watch sci-fi all my life, and I've never associated physic powers with teleportation. Why is teleporting such a big deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T20:33:04-07:00","id":1481,"title":"","content":"Cause it's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T21:48:26-07:00","id":1524,"title":"","content":"While I do not share Telgar's stance on back story and metaplot, I have to agree teleportation IS awesome.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T06:30:15-08:00","id":1703,"title":"","content":"I sort of had the understanding that the backstory of the new Trinity Continuum would not be exactly the same as the old. Perhaps not as different as say CWoD and NWoD, but different none the less.<br /> <br /> Either way since I've sort of gotten the impression that part of the goal with the new Trinity line is to create a setting where you can run games at pretty much ANY point in the timeline of the universe, I would hope that if certain groups have been purged in the default time setting (Chitra Bhanu got wiped out say) that the rules crunch necessary to use them would still be included in the GM section or as an appendix in the back of the book.<br /> <br /> This was something that really bothered me in \u00c6on since it was later heavily implied (at least to my reading) that pretty much ALL the orders saved/hide a couple Quantakinetics after the purge, which meant that there were at least a few left for use as plot characters, but no rules for their powers...<br /> <br /> <br /> All other things aside, one of my favorite parts of NWoD with I hope will be carried over to Trinity Continuum, is the persistence of the &quot;Here's a major plot things, now here are Three viable options, no single one is the absolute correct canon answer nor ever will be.&quot; The VII supplement for V:tR is my ideal for all things dealing with stuff that in CWoD would have been part of the Meta Plot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something like a Chitra Bhanu source book like this. <br /> Chapter 1: Option, the Chibs are all dead. Details of the purge. Plot element: the order heads keep this very hush hush, but the Prometheus Chamber of an order is tied metaphysically to EVERY psion empowered by it. The Chibs are all dead because the other Proxies siezed the Chitra chamber and created a feedback overload that literally cooked all the Quantakinetics brains in the skulls. Further details on Prometheus chambers, further details on fall out from genociding an order, plot seeds for &quot;Oh crud, someone stole the Legion Chamber and now I have a headache&quot;<br /> <br /> Chapter 2: Option, the Chibs were purged, BUT a small number survived, both escapees who were away on secret assignments, and a few kept by other orders as pets/researchers/weapons of last resort. Details on Quantakinetics as a set of powers that basically all revolve around &quot;Interfere with OR bolster Nova powers&quot;. Chibs of this type are only useful in a situation specifically involving direct contact with Novas.<br /> <br /> Chapter 3: Option, the purge happened, but it went bad and 90% of the Chibs escaped. The Proxy EITHER managed to escape with the Prometheus chamber OR the Chamber was captured by the other orders but STOLEN BACK by the aid of a rogue teleporter. Details on Quantakinetics as a set of power that allow Chibs to MIMIC Nova Powers. Chibs of this type are, with a bit of effort, able to manifest Mega-stats, some quantum powers, and other nova abilities for short times. They also, however, generate Taint when using Nova powers. Perhaps MORE than an actual nova. These Chibs are scared, angry, on the run, and just about ready and able to visit their wrath on the world for their betrayal. And they might just decide that Novas aren't so bad after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T09:30:15-08:00","id":1838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=1703#post1703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sort of had the understanding that the backstory of the new Trinity Continuum would not be exactly the same as the old. Perhaps not as different as say CWoD and NWoD, but different none the less.<br /> <br /> Either way since I've sort of gotten the impression that part of the goal with the new Trinity line is to create a setting where you can run games at pretty much ANY point in the timeline of the universe, I would hope that if certain groups have been purged in the default time setting (Chitra Bhanu got wiped out say) that the rules crunch necessary to use them would still be included in the GM section or as an appendix in the back of the book.<br /> <br /> This was something that really bothered me in \u00c6on since it was later heavily implied (at least to my reading) that pretty much ALL the orders saved/hide a couple Quantakinetics after the purge, which meant that there were at least a few left for use as plot characters, but no rules for their powers.....</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, only the Norca were saving Quantakinetics - there's no mention of it in any other order book. Still causes much the same issue, though.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Ian's not been forthcoming on the Quantakinetics' fate in the new edition - there may have been no purge, or psion creation may have been modified so that now any order can create any type of psion (there might still have been a purge, but there'd still be playable Quantakinetics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:07:09-08:00","id":2082,"title":"","content":"We're tweaking the backstory a bit - it will be different, but also still perfectly recognizable. However, there will be a few surprises, and also a few obvious changes (for example, wireless voice and data are no long strictly limited and exceedingly expensive, PCs can have smartphones &amp; AR glasses). However, the big change is that we aren't keeping secrets from the GM. The secrets section of the Aeon core book won't have details on everything, but will give a broad overview of all the actual truths of the setting. Also, future supplements will provide more detail, but won't radically change the setting. The change in setting is more like the difference between cWoD 2nd eds and cWoD Revised, but we aren't going to have an evolving metaplot that will radically alter the setting. As an example of what I'm saying, Aeon will be set shortly after Upeo Wa Macho has returned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:17:47-08:00","id":2096,"title":"","content":"Can we at least get full rules for Quantakinesis somewhere? As far as I know, they never existed in Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T20:49:15-08:00","id":2337,"title":"","content":"I fully support Telgar's request for full details on the Quantakinesis. Even if it would be a Kickstarter goal if that route is taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:16:34-08:00","id":2353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2096#post2096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we at least get full rules for Quantakinesis somewhere? As far as I know, they never existed in Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a hypothetical question. Assuming they never intended to give them rules, what if they just don't have any good ideas about how to do them? Is it better to have them be kinda lame than to not have them at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:41:43-08:00","id":2373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2096#post2096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we at least get full rules for Quantakinesis somewhere? As far as I know, they never existed in Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely plan to eventually put out full rules for QK, as well as more about Chitra Bhanu.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:45:12-08:00","id":2375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2373#post2373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely plan to eventually put out full rules for QK, as well as more about Chitra Bhanu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that answers that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:04:51-08:00","id":2385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2082#post2082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The secrets section of the Aeon core book won't have details on everything, but will give a broad overview of all the actual truths of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you still be using the in-universe background material? Those sections were what really drew me into the original books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:05:41-08:00","id":2386,"title":"","content":"It's the eventually that bums me out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was really hoping to have the corebook for Aeon contain rules for all eight Psi orders. Oh well. At least it'll have teleporters!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T23:14:03-08:00","id":2423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2385#post2385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will you still be using the in-universe background material? Those sections were what really drew me into the original books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emails will remain (it wouldn't feel like the same game w/o them, at least not to me). However, most of the background material will be out of character. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T17:10:53-08:00","id":39699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=1524#post1524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do not share Telgar's stance on back story and metaplot, I have to agree teleportation IS awesome.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an awesome power. But it's a bitch and a half to balance while still keeping fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T21:22:58-08:00","id":40913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=39699#post39699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an awesome power. But it's a bitch and a half to balance while still keeping fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>The balance depends on the players and environment just like it does for the other types, besides the chronic problem of the game system itself threatening to fall apart at higher levels the mechanics of the balance in regard to teleport powers is not much if any worse than it is for the others. Of course how the group interprets the rules makes a difference so the relative effective power of the various psionic aptitudes can be different from group to group.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a complication with the teleporters and quantakinetics in that there are two entirely different balance points for each of the two depending on exactly when the game is set. Pre purge / pre exodus games where the character can openly use their powers they both tend to be slightly on the high side but not overpoweringly so whereas post purge / exodus games mean that they have to masquerade as members of other orders and do things that could be explained as effect overlap with other aptitudes, the use of secondary modes, or else do things with such subtlety that it does not appear that they used psionics to do it at all which limits their power considerably in \u201cpublic\u201d.<br /> <br /> I ran a campaign that had both a Upeo and an \u201cIndia Underground\u201d style Chib in it along with a mix of the usual types that worked out rather well. <br /> <br /> ** Sorry about the length of the post, I would have folded it here with a spoiler tag if I knew how to make one. The gist of it is above so you can skip the rest if you are not interested in the details of how I came to the conclusion above. **<br /> <br /> The teleporter was a prot\u00e9g\u00e9 of Khaldun al-Masna who came from the same kind of Legion background though she grew up in the war-torn American southwest. When, like al-Masna, she was tagged as a latent psi it was unclear whether she was teleporter or seer material so she was sent to the then convalescent semi-retired Legion teleporter for evaluation. In his relatively new (and still unknown outside the Upeo) role as Monitor chief he recognized her potential as a deep cover agent and after recruiting her for it sent word back that no, she was not jumper material, she was primarily a clairsentient candidate with the probability of teleport secondary modes (when she was really the opposite). <br /> <br /> Taking advantage of the rare \u201cblack market\u201d in dunkings and ISRA\u2019s sloppy organizational security, Upeo agents arraigned a carefully orchestrated shell game to have their newly Upeo-dunked mole slipped into the ISRA recovery room and smuggle out the new \u201cunregistered\u201d clear that was actually dunked in the ISRA tank in place of the PC. After ISRA training in the basics of clairvoyance she was sent back to the Legion before anyone noticed that despite a strong psi potential she could not do anything beyond the most basic levels of clairvoyance. <br /> <br /> In the Legion she is an exceptional scout and artillery spotter, her uncanny ability to get into and out of hazardous locations undetected is generally chalked up to her supposed clairvoyant abilities coupled to stealth and climbing/wriggling skills learned in her life in an FSA guerilla warzone. She keeps close ties with her friends in ISRA too and when she is detached to go on \u201cmerc rotation\u201d often works with the Qadiyya, especially on dangerous cases were someone with experience in deadly situations is a plus (and of course it is an excellent place to pick up information on goings on in the Order and elsewhere).<br /> <br /> <br /> She did such a good job of both infiltrating the Legion and keeping an ear to goings on in ISRA that when the ball dropped and the Upeo bugged out it was decided to leave her in place to continue her intelligence gathering and also to look into the looming malevolent presence Atwan so strongly suspected was manipulating the Orders but could not quite put her finger on.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Chib was one of a pair of \u201ctwin cousins\u201d like Patty and Cathy Lane in the old \u201cPatty Duke\u201d show who like the girls in the show looked alike but were quite different in personality and potentials (though also like them they could easily impersonate each other so well that they could even fool their parents). One turned out to be a quantakinetic and the other electrokinetic, one more studious the other more artistic, etc. <br /> <br /> On the fateful day of the purge the two were impersonating each other, with the spark in India spending some time with her boyfriend (one of her cousin\u2019s peers) and the Chib in New York with her American cousin\u2019s family and the arts scene there. Her cousin and parents were killed and in the days following she had several close calls with the intense search for Chitra Bhanu survivors, each one getting closer to detecting her. Worn down by grief, exhausted from nightmare wracked sleep, and constantly near panic she eventually confessed the switch to her uncle and he turned to his employer, Aeon, for help. <br /> <br /> They kept her on ice (literally, in suspended animation), tucked away under Lake Michigan for a few years until the furor of the hunt was long gone. Afterward, since she was more than willing to completely throw her lot in with Aeon they did not keep her locked up though they kept her moving from safehouse to safehouse while she went through training and indoctrination and their study of her while her while they made sure no one picked her trail up. She emerged as a promising young field scientist with supposedly mostly neglected low end electrokinetic powers and an excellent shot at being a science officer on one of the new starships.<br /> <br /> <br /> The campaign started out with the PCs involved in a project that was meant as a mix of potentially valuable exploration and research into the most inaccessible areas of the European badlands with an eye towards improving overall conditions, training for hostile environment exploration and combat, and field testing the technology for that before it is cleared for general deployment, with of course a generous dash of PR for the organizations involved as well.<br /> <br /> In that context there was little problem with balance with the teleport or the quantakinetic powers in either \u201cstealth\u201d mode or full out in the latter part of the campaign. Playing an underground character like that is not for everyone though, it only works well if the player is willing to accept that their power use is limited compared to the others and that they have to concentrate more on skills and equipment use. Later on the campaign moved into space and there was a bit more freedom for the \u201cunderground\u201d characters to use their powers and as I said earlier the balance was still not significantly more difficult than the others.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T11:53:55-08:00","id":45031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2082#post2082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the big change is that we aren't keeping secrets from the GM. The secrets section of the Aeon core book won't have details on everything, but will give a broad overview of all the actual truths of the setting. Also, future supplements will provide more detail, but won't radically change the setting. The change in setting is more like the difference between cWoD 2nd eds and cWoD Revised, but we aren't going to have an evolving metaplot that will radically alter the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best news of all. In retrospect, keeping secrets from the GM (or, in our case, ST) may have been what killed a lot of metaplot-heavy RPGs of the millennium's turn (<b>Trinity</b>, <b>Aberrant</b>, <i>Brave New World</i>\u200b and others I'm probably forgetting); at the very least, it can't have helped sales as much as the publishers who supported the decision thought it would. Quite the reverse, in fact. To paraphrase those DirecTV adverts that keep showing up on my household's Dish Network: When you only reveal the game's metaplot a piece at a time, GMs don't understand the metaplot. When GMs don't understand the metaplot, they can't run the metaplot. When they can't run the metaplot, they don't run the game. When they don't run the game, they don't buy the supplements for it. When they don't buy the supplements, you stop publishing the game. When you stop publishing the game, the rest of the metaplot never gets properly revealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T01:16:09-08:00","id":46136,"title":"","content":"I kind of thought of the metaplot mystery as a kind of game within a game, all the teasers in the color section were more interesting without knowing the whole story. On the other hand it did make it harder in some ways to run a campaign and the one I ran kind of turned into a close parallel of the official metaplot that would have taken some tricky tinkering to get back to the official one if I had tried since there were some fundamental differences in the campaign foundation that I did not know about when I started it.<br /> <br /> It would still be interesting to have that double game setup in one way, but it would most likely cause too many problems to be practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T02:28:01-08:00","id":73105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2082#post2082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're tweaking the backstory a bit - it will be different, but also still perfectly recognizable. However, there will be a few surprises, and also a few obvious changes (for example, wireless voice and data are no long strictly limited and exceedingly expensive, PCs can have smartphones &amp; AR glasses). However, the big change is that we aren't keeping secrets from the GM. The secrets section of the Aeon core book won't have details on everything, but will give a broad overview of all the actual truths of the setting. Also, future supplements will provide more detail, but won't radically change the setting. The change in setting is more like the difference between cWoD 2nd eds and cWoD Revised, but we aren't going to have an evolving metaplot that will radically alter the setting. As an example of what I'm saying, Aeon will be set shortly after Upeo Wa Macho has returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds very positive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T21:36:14-08:00","id":75437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/906-less-plot-more-choices-please?p=2373#post2373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely plan to eventually put out full rules for QK, as well as more about Chitra Bhanu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool.<br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}